If the side length of the cube is \( s \), then the space diagonal is given by: \[
s\sqrt{3} = 1 \implies s = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
\]

The magnitude of this vector is: \[
\left\| \overrightarrow{AO} \times \overrightarrow{AP} \right\| = \sqrt{\left( \frac{1}{12} \right)^2 + \left( -\frac{1}{12} \right)^2 + 0^2} = \sqrt{\frac{1}{144} + \frac{1}{144}} = \sqrt{\frac{2}{144}} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{12}
\]

The area of triangle \( AOP \) is half the magnitude of the cross product: \[
\text{Area of } \triangle AOP = \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{\sqrt{2}}{12} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{24}
\]
